@* Quick-reference modal for COLREGS Rules 13-15 (overtaking / head-on /
   crossing). Opens from the AIS popup's "?" link next to the COLREGS
   row - the previous /help/colregs target navigated AWAY from the map
   AND was broken under the SK plugin mount where the absolute path
   landed at the wrong route. Same dismissal contract as
   LegendOverlay / MapShortcutsOverlay: backdrop click and the [Close]
   button both invoke OnDismiss.

   Intentionally short - this is helm-side first-aid, not a full IRPCS
   course. The "Full reference" link at the bottom takes the helm to
   the standalone HelpColregs page for anything beyond the three
   crossing rules. *@

<div class="shortcuts-overlay" @onclick="OnDismiss">
    <div class="shortcuts-card legend-card colregs-card" @onclick:stopPropagation>
        <h5>COLREGS — quick reference</h5>
        <p class="text-muted" style="font-size: 0.85rem; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">
            Who turns when two vessels approach each other (Rules 13-15, power-driven).
            OnaPlotter classifies the encounter and shows the role on the AIS popup
            + CPA alarm banner.
        </p>

        <ul class="legend-list colregs-list">
            <li>
                <span class="legend-name">Head-on</span>
                <span class="legend-desc">Both vessels altering to <strong>starboard</strong>; pass port-to-port.</span>
            </li>
            <li>
                <span class="legend-name">Overtaking</span>
                <span class="legend-desc">The overtaking vessel keeps clear; the overtaken stands on.</span>
            </li>
            <li>
                <span class="legend-name">Crossing (S)</span>
                <span class="legend-desc">Target on YOUR <strong>starboard</strong> side. You give way - standard move is a starboard turn behind the target's stern.</span>
            </li>
            <li>
                <span class="legend-name">Crossing (P)</span>
                <span class="legend-desc">Target on YOUR <strong>port</strong> side. You stand on - maintain course and speed (Rule 17 lets you manoeuvre once it's clear the give-way vessel isn't acting).</span>
            </li>
        </ul>

        <h6 style="margin-top: 0.75rem; font-size: 0.85rem;">Roles</h6>
        <ul class="legend-list colregs-list">
            <li>
                <span class="legend-name" style="color: var(--sev-danger);">Give way</span>
                <span class="legend-desc">Alter course early and substantially. Audible cue in the OnaPlotter CPA alarm.</span>
            </li>
            <li>
                <span class="legend-name" style="color: var(--sev-ok);">Stand on</span>
                <span class="legend-desc">Maintain course and speed.</span>
            </li>
        </ul>

        <div style="margin-top: 0.75rem; display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center;">
            <a href="help/colregs" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
               style="font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--sk-accent);">
                Full reference &rarr;
            </a>
            <button class="map-btn" @onclick="OnDismiss">Close</button>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public EventCallback OnDismiss { get; set; }
}
